    {
      "id": "b011",
      "chapter": "s2",
      "kind": "narration",
      "display": {
        "en": "Every fraction has two numbers. The bottom number is called the denominator. It tells you how many equal pieces the whole is cut into. The top number is called the numerator. It tells you how many of those pieces you are talking about. So three over four means three slices out of four."
      },
      "spoken": {
        "en": "Every fraction has two numbers. The bottom number is called the denominator. It tells you how many equal pieces the whole is cut into. The top number is called the numerator. It tells you how many of those pieces you are talking about. So three over four means three slices out of four."
      },
